      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Kirk O. Kolbo)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kolbo: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Jennifer Gratz and Patrick Hamacher were denied admission to the University of Michigan's flagship undergraduate institution, the College of Literature and the Science and the Arts under an admissions-- under admissions policies that facially and flagrantly discriminated on the basis of race."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. -- Mr. Kolbo, as a preliminary matter, would you address the question of whether the named plaintiff Patrick Hamacher has standing in this case. He was denied admission, I think, in 1997?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Kirk O. Kolbo)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KOLBO: The transfer admissions policy itself is not before you -- the Court, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (General Theodore B. Olson)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL OLSON: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The University of Michigan admissions program has created a separate path and a separate door for preferred minorities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: First the changes were sufficient to convince the district judge that it was on the other side of the constitutional line?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: It was the same 20 points given -- socioeconomic status also had 20 points?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL OLSON: Well, their argument, A, takes several forms, at one point it's that, at one point, it's the need to get more people elite -- of different backgrounds, it's a -- but what this Court has said that racial preferences, racial stereotyping, which it is, is stigmatizing, it's divisive, it's damaging to the fabric of society, it's damaging to the goal ultimately to eliminate the problems that racial discrimination and racial differences have created."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But remember he has that and gets 20 points for it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What you're saying is that race is individualized consideration?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "University of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PAYTON: The admissions review committee -- about 70 percent of the applications that it reviews in any given year are white student applications that are sent to it. Okay. It can reach its judgment irrespective of whatever happened in the selection index score."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "University of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PAYTON: The design is to make sure we get to the critical mass of the meaningful numbers and given the small pool size we have, the way it operates is as you just described, but that's the way it operates, the design is to make sure we get the critical mass of students that are, in fact, necessary for the educational benefits that we are asserting here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "University of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PAYTON: Yes, I do. I think they do in all sorts of ways. They are certainly producing black students, white students, Hispanic students, Native American students who go out into our communities and change their communities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-516",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f6bff366204163d9750aeba129f9090ace00c8dcff80c34bea6ddba1900f1b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f6bff366204-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
